cle without compromising data integrity is highly valuable. It prevents \"compliance drift\" where researchers skip logging to move faster, potentially jeopardizing the validity of results or legal standing.\n    *   *Alignment with Article 12:* Directly addresses the requirement for automatic recording (Art 12(1)) and specifically handles the fields required for Annex III systems (Art 12(3)).\n\n    *   Is it a research project? No, it's an engineering utility.\n    *   Does it support research? Yes, by automating the \"boring\" part of high-risk AI deployment, allowing researchers to focus on the \"frontier.\"\n    *   Does it have intellectual merit? Low in terms of *novelty*, but high in terms of *operational excellence* for a scientific institution.\n    *   Is it worth committing resources? Yes, because the alternative (per-project manual implementation) is a recurring waste of researcher time and a risk to compliance.\n\n    *   *Rationale:* This proposal eliminates the friction between regulatory compliance and experimental velocity by automating logging at the infrastructure level, allowing researchers to focus on intellectual merit rather than boilerplate instrumentation. Standardizing event capture across prototypes also enhances the reproducibility and auditability of our scientific outputs.\n    *   *Decision:* approve.\n    *   *Promise:* 85 (High because it solves a practical pain point for the research staff and ensures structural compliance, though it's more an engineering win than a theoretical one).",
