urden (\"post-hoc step\") to an engineering standard (CI/CD hook).\n    *   It addresses both \"technical documentation\" (Recital 71) and \"automatic recording of events\" (Article 12).\n    *   It prevents the common failure mode where researchers forget to document a specific version or data tweak, which would be a major compliance breach.\n\n    *   Rationale: Integrating record-keeping directly into the CI/CD pipeline ensures continuous compliance and minimizes the risk of documentation gaps that typically occur during post-hoc reviews. This proactively addresses Article 12's logging requirements and Recital 71's demand for up-to-date technical documentation, protecting the institution from regulatory sanctions.\n    *   Decision: approve.\n    *   Promise: 95 (High confidence because it solves a systemic risk of human error in compliance).",
