ystem vulnerabilities or internal logic that could be exploited (security risk) or lead to accusations of data leakage if the anonymization is reversed (GDPR risk).\n        3.  *Institutional Survival/Resource Allocation:* This proposal suggests using scarce resources to build a public benchmark based on compliance logs. While it's \"nice to have\" for prestige, it doesn't actually solve the legal requirement of Article 12; it creates an *additional* workload (building the anonymization pipeline) on top of the mandatory logging system.\n        4.  *The Logic Error:* The idea that public release replaces regulatory reporting is a dangerous legal fallacy.\n\n    *   The proposal conflates *scientific transparency* with *regulatory compliance*.\n    *   It creates unnecessary GDPR and security risks by publishing sensitive operational data (even if processed).\n    *   It does not actually fulfill the requirements of Article 12 for audit purposes.",
